2. Decompiled game code (no license granted)

   Everything else — in particular src/ (outside src/port/), courses/, data/,
   include/, asm/, assets/ and the build files inherited from the
   decompilation — is the decompiled code and data layout of Mario Kart 64,
   produced by the n64decomp/mk64 project. It is the copyrighted work of
   Nintendo. No license to it is granted or implied by this repository; it is
   distributed for the purposes of preservation and interoperability, and this
   repository does not include the game's assets.

3. Code adapted from other ports

   src/port/gfx/gfx_pc.c, src/port/gfx/gfx_cc.c and src/port/audio/mixer.c
   are adapted from sm64-port (https://github.com/sm64-port/sm64-port), which
   publishes no license; they are used here on the same basis as that project.
   src/port/psp/gfx_scegu.c (the sceGu rendering backend) derives from the PSP
   port of sm64-port by Hayden Kowalchuk, on the same basis.
   Parts of the audio mixer behaviour follow SpaghettiKart
   (https://github.com/HarbourMasters/SpaghettiKart).

   src/port/psp/psp_texture_manager.c and psp_texture_manager.h are
   Copyright (c) 2020 Hayden Kowalchuk, BSD 3-Clause License
   (http://www.opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause); the notice in the files
   must be kept in redistributions.

